    "polynomial_semantics": "Each tabulated element is evaluated as a0 + a1*t + a2*t^2 + a3*t^3, where t is TDT/TT hours from the event's t0_tt_jd. NASA states that each polynomial is fitted at five equally spaced epochs over the six-hour interval t0 +/- 3 hours.",
    "coordinate_semantics": "x and y are the lunar-shadow-axis coordinates on the geocentric fundamental plane, with +x east and +y north. x, y, l1, and l2 are in Earth equatorial radii; d and mu are in degrees; tan_f1 and tan_f2 are dimensionless. mu comparisons are circular modulo 360 degrees. NASA's sign convention makes l2 negative for an umbral/total cone and positive for an antumbral/annular cone.",
    "reference_model_note": "These published NASA/GSFC rows use the declared VSOP87/ELP2000-82 eclipse-catalog ephemerides and k1/k2 lunar-radius conventions. They are an external cross-model reference for Moira's DE441-native Earth-reception geometry and physical mean-limb radii, not DE441 coefficients and not uncertainty bounds.",
